From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 22:14:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Write the bytes at the ends with their halfword on the
 Nintendo DS

VRAM and the RAM of the GBA slot ignore byte writes, so the generic
memcpy, memmove and memset lose the bytes at the ends of copies and
fills there. The DS versions move words, eight at a time, or halfwords
and write those bytes with their halfword. They are ARM code, which
the ARM9 runs from ITCM.
---
